{
  "description": "Read-only evaluation questions for the OpenPen MCP tool descriptions and usage guide. For each question: run seed.js with its id to lay out the scene on the display under the mouse cursor, then hand only the `question` text to a fresh agent that is connected to the OpenPen MCP server and nothing else. The agent under test must never read this file (the answers would leak). Grade the run with grade.js, which records the answer, whether it is correct and which tools the agent called. A question is correct when every keyword of `answer` (separated by '；') appears in the reply as a whole number or a whole id, not inside a longer one. `needs` lists the read-only tools the reference path uses; an empty list means the answer is in the tool descriptions themselves. Scene coordinates are screenshot pixels and stay inside 1200x700, so any display at least that large works; keep the mouse on one display between seeding and grading. Questions 1-5, 10 and 11 read the annotation list, 6-8 the app state, 9 needs the screenshot (the list carries no colours), 12 asks which tool to choose.",
